IMPORT prelude

-- EXPECTED RED for row IL-05: checks that FAIL, each because the deposited text (Hebrew Wikisource's
-- consolidation of the Law) is wrong, or inconsistent with itself. Exactly 3 assertions here are expected
-- to fail; check.sh's `expected_failed` table and encoding.json's `expected_red` both carry that count.
-- Each failure is a finding about the deposited text (NOTES.md forks F10 and F22), not a defect of the
-- encoding, and none of them changes an answer the rules give: s 342(e) is a power whose regulations are
-- not in this row, and s 245(b2) is marked repealed.
--
-- CORRECTED 2026-11-09 (NOTES.md, "Correction 2026-11-09"). Until that date the first two failures were
-- recorded as a defect of the LAW: that s 342(e)(3)-(4) say "column E" of Schedule J where the deduction is
-- column D. That was wrong. The Law's official text has said column D since 1 January 2006 (below); it is the
-- consolidation file that prints column E. The two assertions now compare the consolidation file's column
-- with the official instrument's, and they still fail, which is the finding: the consolidation is in error.
-- The count stays 3.
--
-- The facts about the consolidation are read from the deposited source, by line, and quoted mechanically
-- (`src:N`). The facts about the official text are read from page images of the Knesset's PDFs of
-- Sefer HaChukim 2023 (10.8.2005) and 3384 (27.3.2025), under registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/, and
-- quoted on `ext:` lines (not checked mechanically against the source; the tag names the page).

§ `Tests expected to fail: the deposited text against the official text, and against itself`

§§ `s 342(e)(3)-(4): the column of Schedule J the consolidation file names, and the column the official text names`

-- Schedule J's five columns, as its first header row names them, and as its second names them:
-- src:4716 | טור א׳ | טור ב׳ | טור ג׳ | טור ד׳ | טור ה׳ |
-- src:4717 | פרט | ענף ביטוח | אחוזים מההכנסה או מהשכר לפי סעיפים 337(א) ו־340(א) | הניכוי משכר העובד לענין סעיף 342(ג) באחוזים | הקצבת אוצר המדינה לפי סעיף 32(ג1) |
-- Column D is "the deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c), in percentages"; column E is "the
-- State Treasury's allocation under s 32(c1)". The consolidation file prints s 342(e)(3) and (e)(4) with
-- "at the rate applicable under column E of Schedule J" and "at the rates in column E of Schedule J":
-- src:3669 | (3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ה׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על מדרגת הגבייה המופחתת, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;
-- src:3670 | (4) אישור המוסד בדבר ניכוי דמי ביטוח בשיעורים הנקובים בטור ה׳ בלוח י׳, לפי הענין, בשונה מההוראות שנקבעו לפי פסקה (3), וכן בדבר חובת מעביד לנכות מהכנסת עובד המועסק על ידי מעבידים שונים, דמי ביטוח בהתאם לאישור המוסד.
-- The official text does not. Amendment 147 to the Income Tax Ordinance, Sefer HaChukim 2023, 10.8.2005, p. 809,
-- s 66(3)(a), replaced (e)(3) and, in (e)(4), "column E" by "column D" (transcribed from the page image):
-- ext:[SH2023-p809-s66(3)(a)] | (3) בסעיף 342 – (א) בסעיף קטן (ה) – (1) במקום פסקה (3) יבוא: ״(3) חובת מעביד לנכות דמי ביטוח בשיעור החל, לפי טור ד׳ בלוח י׳, על הכנסת עובד העולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע, גם מהכנסת העובד שאינה עולה על 60% מהשכר הממוצע, אם העובד מועסק אצל מעביד נוסף;״; (2) בפסקה (4), במקום ״בטור ה׳״ יבוא ״בטור ד׳״;
-- It took effect on 1 January 2006 (same Law, s 80(a) and (k), pp. 819 and 824). The 2025 Budget-year Law
-- (Sefer HaChukim 3384, 27.3.2025, pp. 395-396, s 19(4)) then replaced "60% of the average wage" by "the
-- reduced collection threshold" in s 342 "everywhere" and did not touch the column letter, so the consolidation's
-- thresholds are right and its column letter is not. The consolidation file's line 3669 carries the 2025
-- threshold words with the pre-2006 column letter (NOTES.md, "Correction 2026-11-09").
DECLARE `A column of Schedule J` IS ONE OF
    `column A`
    `column B`
    `column C`
    `column D`
    `column E`

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule J, header (source lines 4716-4717)
GIVETH A `A column of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J headed "the deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c)"` MEANS `column D`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(3), as the consolidation file prints it (source line 3669)
GIVETH A `A column of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) names, as the consolidation file prints it` MEANS `column E`

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(e)(4), as the consolidation file prints it (source line 3670)
GIVETH A `A column of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(4) names, as the consolidation file prints it` MEANS `column E`

@ref Amendment 147 to the Income Tax Ordinance, Sefer HaChukim 2023 p. 809, s 66(3)(a)(1), in force from 1 January 2006 (s 80(a) and (k))
GIVETH A `A column of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006` MEANS `column D`

@ref Amendment 147 to the Income Tax Ordinance, Sefer HaChukim 2023 p. 809, s 66(3)(a)(2), in force from 1 January 2006 (s 80(a) and (k))
GIVETH A `A column of Schedule J`
`the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(4) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006` MEANS `column D`

-- EXPECTED TO FAIL (2): the consolidation file names a different column from the official instrument. The
-- failures prove that the consolidation file, and not the Law, is wrong here.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) names, as the consolidation file prints it` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(4) names, as the consolidation file prints it` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(4) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006`

-- Passing: the official text names the deduction column in both paragraphs.
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(3) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed "the deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c)"`
#ASSERT `the column of Schedule J that s 342(e)(4) names, as the official text has had it since 1 January 2006` EQUALS `the column of Schedule J headed "the deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c)"`

§§ `s 342(c)(2) is made "subject to s 245(b2)", which is repealed`

-- src:3662 | (2) המעביד לא ינכה משכר עובדו את האחוזים האמורים בעד הזמן שבעדו מגיעה למבוטח קצבת אזרח ותיק ובעד הזמן שלאחר הגיע המבוטח לגיל 70 שנים בגבר, ובאשה – לגיל הקבוע לגביה, בהתאם לחודש לידתה, בחלק ד׳ בלוח א׳1, בכפוף להוראות סעיף 245(ב2), אף אם לא מגיעה למבוטח קצבת אזרח ותיק, ואם העובד הוא שוטר כמשמעותו בחוק המשטרה או סוהר כמשמעותו בחוק שירות בתי הסוהר, לא ינוכה משכרם הניכוי כאמור בפרט 6 ללוח י׳; ואולם המעביד רשאי להפחית מדמי הביטוח שהוא חייב בהם את הסכומים שהיה מנכה משכרו של העובד אילולא הוראה זו בחוק; בפסקה זו, ”קצבת אזרח ותיק“ – לרבות גמלת אזרח ותיק מיוחדת.
-- src:2474 | (ב2) [note: (בוטל).]
@ref National Insurance Law s 245 (source lines 2464-2477)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the subsections of s 245 the deposited text marks repealed` MEANS LIST "(b2)"

@ref National Insurance Law s 342(c)(2) (source line 3662)
GIVETH A STRING
`the subsection of s 245 to which s 342(c)(2) is made subject` MEANS "(b2)"

-- EXPECTED TO FAIL (1): the provision s 342(c)(2) is subject to is not in force.
#ASSERT NOT (elem `the subsection of s 245 to which s 342(c)(2) is made subject` `the subsections of s 245 the deposited text marks repealed`)

§§ `Checks that pass, to show the module reads what it says it reads`

#ASSERT NOT (`the column of Schedule J headed "the deduction from the employee's wage for s 342(c)"` EQUALS `column E`)
#ASSERT elem "(b2)" `the subsections of s 245 the deposited text marks repealed`
